WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:01.570
I started getting short of breath,

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:06.260
so definitely does attack
your respiratory system,

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:08.050
and it hits it hard.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:10.270
So I think, like,

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:11.800
that was one of the worst symptoms,

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.060
because I woke up in
the middle of the night,

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:17.060
and I was disoriented. I
wasn't able to breathe.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.190
I had a very high fever.

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:22.510
I also had started to pick up a dry cough.

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:27.440
Those are the only two signs
of anything coronavirus.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.520
Unlike other colds and the flu that I had,

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:33.660
there was no headache,
no sneezing, no sniffles,

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:36.430
no sore throat, no body aches,

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:39.840
and even with that high
fever, no chills and sweats

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.000
that you usually get, that hot and cold.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.480
I wasn't able to get anybody's attention,

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.530
and I think at that point,
you start sitting down

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:48.890
and having a conversation
with yourself, like,

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:51.550
OK, this is it for me.

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.100
This is it for me and my children.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.770
I won't ever see them again-type of thing.

00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:59.420
But I thank God that he was with me,

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:02.420
was able to wake him
up, wake my husband up

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:04.940
to let him know that
something wasn't right.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:06.060
Biocontainment was weird.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.330
I spent 10 days in there.

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:12.110
I was hooked up to all kinds of monitors.

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:15.240
Anyone entering my biocontainment,

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.800
it was like Neil Armstrong
landing on the moon.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.260
They had full biocontainment suits on,

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:22.990
three layers of gloves,

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:25.860
a motor in their back to provide air,

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:29.110
duct tape all around, sealing off anything

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:32.130
that could possibly expose themselves.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:35.040
I'm quite baffled as to why
people are interested at all.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.520
I'm just this guy that's
got a positive diagnosis

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.490
with no symptoms stuck at home,

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:45.490
but I guess people are fearful,
and I'm sad about that.

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:48.587
I think I'm proof that even
if you catch the virus,

00:01:48.587 --> 00:01:50.770
you can be just fine.

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:52.820
When I first got here, they
wasn't going to test me

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:54.340
because I didn't fit the criteria.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:57.500
After some CAT scans
and a couple of tests,

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.460
they decided to go ahead and test me,

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.980
and they came back and they
told me that I tested positive.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:05.313
My family is on 14-day quarantine.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:07.640
I haven't seen my children,

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:12.040
haven't seen my husband in days now.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:14.290
But there was nothing they could give me

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:18.343
other than ibuprofen and
gallons and gallons of Gatorade.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:22.720
I kid that I've been through
every flavor of the rainbow

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:25.450
of Gatorade multiple amounts of times.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.530
The light blue is the bomb.

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:30.410
Stay away from the grape. That's nasty.

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:34.020
There is no treatment for coronavirus,

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.930
so what they're treating is,
they can treat a symptom.

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:40.060
So if I have a fever, they
can treat it with Tylenol.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:43.180
If I have a cough, they can
treat it with cough medicine.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:46.460
But my body has to fight it off,

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:50.530
so I have to take the time to rest,

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:52.100
make sure that I'm trying to keep down

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:56.160
as much food as I can, and
let my body do its job.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:59.550
I've been here, I think
I lost about 15 pounds,

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:00.990
so I don't know what I'll be looking like

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:02.240
when I get up out of here.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:04.700
I got to get my hair done, you all.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:06.450
Talk about my bonnet.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:08.050
It feels quite surreal

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:10.530
to be part of this huge thing, actually.

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:13.750
I step back and, you know,
realize that, you know,

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:14.900
I see it's on the news.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:17.310
It just dominates the
headlines everywhere.

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:18.320
We were out there.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:20.970
There was a lot of hate that came at us.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:23.840
There were some very
elaborate death threats

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:27.100
that mounted and got worse
as the days progressed,

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:29.140
as people learned that
the State Department

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:31.520
was going to allow us back to the States.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:33.150
Everybody's making jokes about it.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.570
I don't take it personal.

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:36.260
I think the only thing
that kind of bothered me

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:38.383
was to see myself on the news,

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:43.230
to see my local news station, you know,

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:45.240
speak of this situation,

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:49.233
but not even know wholeheartedly,
like, what was going on.

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:53.560
It's a lot scarier when
you see it on the TV

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:57.230
or when you read about it
than what it actually is. But

00:03:57.230 --> 00:04:00.180
I'm not going to sit up here
and pretend like it's a joke.

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:06.230
Definitely has taken
me away from my family,

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:08.650
gave me some breathing problems,

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:11.880
and sat me down for a
while to reevaluate myself,

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:14.970
and kind of, you know, my life.

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:18.210
I know after this, you know,
I want to get out and do more.

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:20.840
All along, we were making
lemonade out of lemons,

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:24.180
looking at the glass half
full, not half empty,

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:27.500
living for the present, not
worrying about the past,

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:30.300
and also not focusing on the future

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:32.630
because all of that
was out of our control.

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:36.420
Stress is the biggest, biggest contributor

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:39.480
to battling the immune system,

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:42.110
and it's not good for the immune system.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:45.880
So keeping our stress
level down was important.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:47.570
So just make sure that you guys

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:49.167
are keeping your kids safe,

00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:52.333
and you're keeping yourself safe as well.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.830
That's the best advice
that I can give anybody.

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:58.440
Just make sure that you all are
paying attention to your body.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:00.950
Your body will let you know
when something is wrong,

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:03.870
and if it's telling you something's wrong,

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.520
then go ahead and get tested.

